cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these certified bounds or the certificate machinery, please cite
  this repository.
title: >-
  Certified bounds for covering the unit disk with 100 equal circles
  (r_D(100): 0.1066235 <= r_D(100) <= 0.1170862)
authors:
  - family-names: "<你的姓>"
    given-names: "<你的名>"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/<可选，没有就删掉这行>"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-27"
abstract: >-
  Certified two-sided bounds for the smallest radius r_D(100) such that 100
  equal circles cover the unit disk. Upper bound 125599387/2^30 = 0.1170862
  via an explicit rational-center construction with an integer quadtree
  covering certificate (4.20% below the previously published value 1/sqrt(67));
  lower bound 0.1066235 via a K=320-ring measure LP with cutting planes and a
  frozen-measure rigorous sup protocol. A rotation-averaging theorem proves
  the radial family is optimal among all Borel probability measures, so
  0.10664 is the exact ceiling of every measure/duality argument. All
  certificates are machine-verifiable; the covering verifier has zero
  dependencies.
keywords:
  - circle covering
  - covering radius
  - certified bounds
  - unit disk covering
  - computational geometry
  - integer arithmetic certificates
